      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "This would be especially useful for face tracking. Atm face tracking apps send their float values as 3 or 4 boolians through OSC so they are directly synced that way, and then converted to floats on remote clients. This makes face tracking animators way more complex than they need to be, making it more difficult for users to customize and fine tune the systems.\n\nIt's especially annoying when trying to debug face tracking, and you have to scroll through 4 times the variables in debug menus and those drop your framerate to nauseating levels.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
